 36NE c  Search for the observation of {+36}Ne nuclide proved negative          
 36NE2c  (2025Ku15, 2022Ah02, 2019Ah07), thus suggesting that {+36}Ne is unbound
 36NE3c  towards neutron emission.                                              
 36NE c  No Q-values from systematics are available in 2021Wa16                 
 36NE c  2025Ku15 (also 2022Ah02, 2019Ah07): E=345 MeV/nucleon {+48}Ca beam was 
 36NE2c  produced from the RIBF accelerator complex at RIKEN. Projectile        
 36NE3c  fragments were separated and identified in flight using the            
 36NE4c  large-acceptance two-stage separator BigRIPS spectrometer by           
 36NE5c  tof-B|p-|DE method. Measured reaction products. Deduced atomic number  
 36NE6c  (Z) versus atomic mass/atomic number (A/Z) particle-identification     
 36NE7c  plot. No events were observed for {+36}Ne, implying that this nuclide  
 36NE8c  is unbound towards neutron emission. Estimated counts (2019Ah07) were  
 36NE9c  15.5 {I47} from EPAX 2.15 reaction model calculations, and 5.03 {I96}  
 36NEAc  from systematics of Q values using LISE++ simulations, with optimum    
 36NEBc  setting on total of {+33}F, and {+36}Ne+{+39}Na.                       
 36NE d  Nuclear structure calculations (levels, bands, binding energy, radii,  
 36NE2d  separation energies, transition strengths, etc): 2023Ra22, 2021Ch70,   
 36NE3d  2020Ts03, 2020Mi15, 2020Ch21, 2020An13, 2019Sa58, 2014Ca21, 2013Zh50,  
 36NE4d  2012Po15, 2010Zh23, 2008Wi11, 2005Ch71, 2004Lu10, 2002Mi14, 2002Ka73,  
 36NE5d  2001Pe15, 2001Na31, 2001Go37, 2000St04, 1999Si13, 1998Vr02, 1998St18,  
 36NE6d  1998La02, 1997Pa38                                                     
