 36MG c  2014Mi09: E=44.5 MeV/nucleon secondary beam was produced by            
 36MG2c  fragmentation of 63 MeV/nucleon {+48}Ca primary beam with {+181}Ta and 
 36MG3c  enriched {+64}Ni target foils of 150 |mm and 200 |mm thicknesses,      
 36MG4c  respectively at RFQ-RILAC-CSM-RRC accelerator at RIKEN facility.       
 36MG5c  Fragments were separated and identified by RIPS fragment separator. THe
 36MG6c  secondary target was liquid hydrogen (CRYPTA). The scattered particles 
 36MG7c  were analyzed by the TOMBEE spectrometer consisting of a               
 36MG8c  superconducting triplet quadrupole, plastic scintillator, and a |DE-E  
 36MG9c  telescope of a silicon detector and a NaI(Tl) detector. |g rays were   
 36MGAc  detected with the DALI2 array of 160 NaI(Tl) detectors. Measured E|g,  
 36MGBc  I|g, |g|g-coin, particle-|g-coin, |s. Deduced levels, deformation      
 36MGCc  lengths and |b{-2} deformation parameter from the analysis of measured 
 36MGDc  |s by coupled-channel calculations with the ECIS97 computer code, and  
 36MGEc  WP09 global potential. Comparison with shell-model (SDPF-M)            
 36MGFc  calculations, and with previous experimental results                   
 36MG cG $|g rays from {+35}Mg formed in neutron-removal channel were seen      
 36MG2cG (Figure 8c in 2014Mi09) at 446, 621 and 670 keV.                       
