 36MG c  2024Ma28: E=140 MeV/nucleon {+48}Ca beam was produced from the         
 36MG2c  cyclotron at NSCL. Target was 846 mg/cm{+2} {+9}Be. Fragments were     
 36MG3c  separated with the A1900 separator and implanted into a 12-mm thick YSO
 36MG4c  detector. Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g-coin, |g(t), neutrons using three    
 36MG5c  HPGe detectors and 48 VANDLE modules. Deduced levels, isomer T{-1/2}   
 36MG c  2023Lu07: E=140 MeV/nucleon {+48}Ca beam was produced from the         
 36MG2c  cyclotron at NSCL. Fragments were separated by the A1900 separator and 
 36MG3c  delivered to the NSCL |b-decay station. Separated ions were implanted  
 36MG4c  in a CeBr{-3} scintillator detector which was coupled to a             
 36MG5c  position-sensitive photomultiplier tube (PSPMT), and surrounded by the 
 36MG6c  16 segmented SeGa array of Ge detectors, and 15 LaBr3 detectors.       
 36MG7c  Measured E|g, ion-|b-|g time correlation. Deduced {+36}Mg T{-1/2}      
 36MG c  2022Cr03: E=172.3 MeV/nucleon {+48}Ca beam was produced from the FRIB  
 36MG2c  LINAC. Fragments were separated by the ARIS separator and delivered to 
 36MG3c  the FRIB decay station (FDSi) and implanted into a fast-response YSO   
 36MG4c  scintillation detector sandwiched by two plastic scintillator veto     
 36MG5c  detectors and surrounded by 11 HPGe clover detectors and 15 fast-timing
 36MG6c  LaBr{-3} detectors. Measured ion-decay time correlation. Deduced       
 36MG7c  {+36}Mg T{-1/2}                                                        
 36MG c  2004Gr20, 2003Gr22: {+36}Mg from fragmentation of 60 MeV/nucleon       
 36MG2c  {+48}Ca beam with {+9}Be target, time-of-flight and energy loss methods
 36MG3c  to identify fragments, LISE-3 spectrometer at GANIL. Measured ion-decay
 36MG4c  time correlation. Deduced {+36}Mg T{-1/2}                              
