 36SI c  2015St14: Al ions were produced by fragmentation of a 345 MeV/nucleon  
 36SI2c  {+48}Ca beam from the RIBF facility at RIKEN on a 15 mm beryllium      
 36SI3c  target. Fragments were separated and identified using the BigRIPS      
 36SI4c  spectrometer and the zero-degree spectrometer (ZDS), with energy loss  
 36SI5c  measured by a multi-sampling ionization chamber (MUSIC) and positions  
 36SI6c  by PPACs. The selected ions were implanted into the CAITEN detector    
 36SI7c  (Cylindrical Active Implantation Target for Exotic Nuclei), consisting 
 36SI8c  of a segmented movable hollow-cylindrical-shape plastic scintillator   
 36SI9c  and a stationary ring of 24 position-sensitive photomultiplier tubes   
 36SIAc  (PSPMTs). |g rays were detected by three HPGe detectors. Measured E|g, 
 36SIBc  I|g, implantation-decay-correlation, |b|g-coin, |g|g-coin, |b|g(t).    
 36SICc  Deduced levels, J, |p, half-life. Comparison with shell-model          
 36SIDc  calculations.                                                          
 36SI c  2023Og04: {+37}Al ions were produced by fragmentation of a 140         
 36SI2c  MeV/nucleon {+48}Ca beam from the Coupled Cyclotron Facility (CCF) of  
 36SI3c  NSCL at Michigan State University on a 642 mg/cm{+2} {+9}Be target.    
 36SI4c  Fragments were separated and identified using the A1900 spectrometer on
 36SI5c  an event-by-event basis according to energy loss and time-of-flight    
 36SI6c  information. The selected ions were implanted into a 51mm|*51mm|*3mm   
 36SI7c  CeBr{-3} detector and |b-delayed |g rays were detected with an array of
 36SI8c  15 LaBr{-3}(Ce) detectors in a ring at 90|' and the Segmented Germanium
 36SI9c  Array (SeGA) of 16 HPGe detectors in two concentric rings in the       
 36SIAc  Beta-SeGA configuration. Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g-coin, |b|g-coin.      
 36SI c  2019Ab06: {+37}Al source was produced by fragmentation of a 140        
 36SI2c  MeV/nucleon {+48}Ca primary beam on a {+9}Be target at NSCL. Fragments 
 36SI3c  were selected with the A1900 separator and selected ions were delivered
 36SI4c  to the decay station and implanted into a GeDSSD detector. |g rays were
 36SI5c  detected the SeGA array of 16 HPGe detectors. Measured E|g, I|g,       
 36SI6c  |g|g-coin, implant-|g(t). Deduced parent T{-1/2}. 2019Ab06 show        
 36SI7c  observed |g rays of {+36}Si in Fig.2 without labels.                   
