 36P  c  2015Ch56: E=215 MeV {+36}S beam was produced using the combination of  
 36P 2c  XTU tandem Van de Graaff accelerator and ALPI superconducting linear   
 36P 3c  accelerator at the INFN Legnaro National Laboratory, Italy. Target was 
 36P 4c  99.7% enriched {+208}Pb with a thickness of 300 |mg/cm{+2} on a 20     
 36P 5c  |mg/cm{+2} carbon backing. Fragments were separated and identified by  
 36P 6c  the PRISMA spectrometer and |g rays were detected with the CLARA array 
 36P 7c  of 25 EUROBALL escape-suppressed HPGe clover detectors. Measured E|g,  
 36P 8c  I|g. Deduced levels, J,|p. Comparisons with shell-model calculations.  
 36P  c  2019Gr08: E=225 MeV {+36}S beam was provided by Tandem-ALPI accelerator
 36P 2c  complex at the INFN Legnaro National Laboratory. Target was 99.7%      
 36P 3c  enriched in {+208}Pb with a thickness of 1 mg/cm{+2} deposited on 1    
 36P 4c  mg/cm{+2} Nb backing. Projectile-like fragments were separated and     
 36P 5c  identified by the PRISMA magnetic spectrometer. |g rays were detected  
 36P 6c  with the AGATA demonstrator array of five triple cluster modules of    
 36P 7c  36-fold segmented Ge crystals. Measured E|g, {+36}P-|g-coin,           
 36P 8c  Doppler-shift recoil distances. Deduced levels, T{-1/2}. Comparison    
 36P 9c  with shell-model calculations using PSDPF effective interaction.       
