 36S 2c  Munich Lamb-shift polarized ion source and Munich tandem accelerator.  
 36S 3c  The target was a cylindrical gas cell (50 mm diameter) filled with     
 36S 4c  H{-2}S enriched to 82.2% in {+36}S at a pressure of |?30 mb, with 100- 
 36S 5c  and 300-|mg/cm{+2} Ti entrance and exit windows. Scattered deuterons   
 36S 6c  were momentum analyzed with the Munich Q3D magnetic spectrograph and   
 36S 7c  detected in a 1.2-m-long position-sensitive focal-plane detector       
 36S 8c  consisting of two single-wire proportional counters backed by a plastic
 36S 9c  scintillator. Measured |s(E{-d},|q) and vector analyzing powers        
 36S Ac  A{-y}(|q) at |q=15|'-110|'. Deduced hadronic transition moments from   
 36S Bc  ECIS79-coupled-channels analysis. Also measured {+36}S(pol d,p){+37}S  
