 36CL c  Includes {+35}Cl(pol n,|g) reaction (1976Sp06,1969Ko05,1970Ei03)       
 36CL c  The level scheme and placements of |g rays are taken from 1982Kr12,    
 36CL2c  unless otherwise noted. Placements are also available in 1976Sp06 and  
 36CL3c  1981Ke02 and noted under comments if different.                        
 36CL c  1982Kr12: thermal neutrons were produced from the high-flux reactor of 
 36CL2c  the Institut Laue-Langevin. Target was KCl of natural chlorine. |g rays
 36CL3c  were detected with the curved-crystal spectrometers GAMS 1 and GAMS 2/3
 36CL4c  (for E|g up to 1.6 MeV), a Ge(Li) detector (for E|g=1.6 MeV to 3.0     
 36CL5c  MeV), and the ILL pair spectrometer (for E|g>3.0 MeV) consisting of a  
 36CL6c  Ge(Li) diode and two NaI(Tl) detectors. Measured E|g, I|g. Deduced     
 36CL7c  levels, J, |p. Report 393 |g rays. Absolute I|g values are obtained by 
 36CL8c  normalizing the sum of all observed g.s. transition to 100             
 36CL c  1976Sp06: thermal neutrons were produced from the reactor Centrum      
 36CL2c  Netherland. Target was natural {+35}Cl. |g rays were detected with a   
 36CL3c  pair spectrometer consisting of two NaI crystals and a Ge(Li) detector.
 36CL4c  Measured E|g, I|g. Deduced levels, J, |p, precise Q-value, |g-ray      
 36CL5c  branching ratios. Report 421 |g rays. Absolute I|g values are obtained 
 36CL6c  by normalizing the sum of I|g|*E|g of all |grays to 100|*Q-value. Also 
 36CL7c  includes (pol n,|g) measurement.                                       
 36CL c  1981Ke02: thermal neutrons were produced from McMaster University      
 36CL2c  Nuclear Reactor. Target was NH{-4}Cl. |g rays were detected with a pair
 36CL3c  spectrometer with an intrinsic Ge detector as the central detector.    
 36CL4c  Measured E|g, I|g. Deduced levels, %I|g. Report 234 |g rays. The       
 36CL5c  authors uses %I|g values of E|g<1600 keV from 1976Sp06 with their I|g  
 36CL6c  values of E|g above 1600 from their measurement for I|g normalization  
 36CL7c  using |S[I|g|*E|g]=100|*Q-value to obtained their reported absolute I|g
 36CL8c  values. See also the earlier work from the same lab in 1972Is14 (137 |g
 36CL9c  rays), 1970Hu03 (130 |g rays), 1966Hu08 (Q-value), 1980Is02 (Q-value)  
 36CL c                                                                         
 36CL c  2020Cr02: thermal neutrons from a high-flux ILL reactor. Target was    
 36CL2c  NaCl crystalline. |g rays were detected with the FIPPS array consisting
 36CL3c  of 8 HPGe detectors. Measured E|g, |g lineshape. Deduced level         
 36CL4c  lifetimes using the GRIDSA method (Gamma Ray Induced Doppler Shift     
 36CL5c  Attenuation)                                                           
 36CL c  2006De21 (also 2000De25): thermal neutrons from a high-flux ILL        
 36CL2c  reactor. Measured E|g, I|g, with the GAMS4 flat-crystal spectrometer.  
 36CL3c  Report 5 |g rays. See also 1985Ke04 for their earlier measurements     
 36CL4c  using the GAMS4 in its early stage. 2006De21 state that some values    
 36CL5c  from 1985Ke04 need to be corrected for changes in the fundamental      
 36CL6c  constants and known errors in the lattice spacing of the crystals.     
 36CL d  2006De21 supersede 2005BeZT, 2005DeZW, 2005JeZY                        
 36CL c  2004Mo01: thermal neutrons were produced from the Budapest PGAA        
 36CL2c  facility. Target was thin polyvinyl chloride. |g rays were detected    
 36CL3c  with a HPGe-BGO Compton-suppressed spectrometer. Measured E|g, I|g.    
 36CL4c  Deduced %I|g. Report 36 |g rays. 2004Mo01 give a detailed comparison of
 36CL5c  %I|g values from several major references and the normalization        
 36CL6c  methods. See 2004Mo01 for the details. The authors state that about 300
 36CL7c  |g rays of {+36}Cl were identified but only 37 |g rays are reported in 
 36CL8c  the paper. Absolute I|g values are obtained by normalizing the sum of  
 36CL9c  all observed g.s. transition intensities to 100                        
 36CL d  2004Mo01 supersede 2002MoZP                                            
 36CL c  1997Ve03: thermal neutrons were produced from t the IEA-R1 2 MW        
 36CL2c  research reactor of IPEN, Brazil. |g rays were detected with a pair    
 36CL3c  spectrometer consisting of two NaI(Tl) scintillators and a Ge(Li)      
 36CL4c  detectors. Measured E|g, I|g. Deduced %I|g. Report 50 |g rays. Absolute
 36CL5c  %I|g values were obtained by measuring |g rays of {+35}Cl(n,|g) mixed  
 36CL6c  with {+14}N(n,|g) and using the ratio of the known cross-sections of   
 36CL7c  two reactions.                                                         
 36CL c  1996Co16: thermal neutrons were produced from the BRI reactor of the   
 36CL2c  SCK, Mol (Belgium). |g rays were detected with Ge(Li) detectors and an 
 36CL3c  NaI(Tl) annulus. Measured E|g, I|g. Deduced %I|g. Report 24 |g rays.   
 36CL4c  Absolute I|g values are obtained by normalizing the sum of all observed
 36CL5c  g.s. transition to 100                                                 
 36CL c  2000Ra36: thermal neutrons were produced from the JRR-3M reactor at the
 36CL2c  Japan Atomic Energy Research Institute (JAERI). |g rays were detected  
 36CL3c  with a large-volume Ge detector. Measured E|g, I|g. Deduced absolute   
 36CL4c  I|g. Report 17 |g rays. The authors obtained their absolute I|g values 
 36CL5c  by normalizing the sum of all their observed |g intensities to the sum 
 36CL6c  of corresponding |g rays in 1996Co16. Their %I|g values are considered 
 36CL7c  less independent and therefore are not considered for average by the   
 36CL8c  evaluator.                                                             
 36CL c  1992Ku17: re-analysis of GRID results in 1991Ul02, by using a molecular
 36CL2c  dynamics simulation of slowing down of nuclei produced in thermal      
 36CL3c  neutron capture                                                        
 36CL c  1991Ul02: thermal neutrons were from the ILL high flux reactor. |g rays
 36CL2c  were detected with the GAMS4 spectrometer equipped with two Si single  
 36CL3c  crystals. Measured E|g, |g lineshape. Deduced level lifetimes using the
 36CL4c  GRID method (Gamma Ray Induced Doppler broadening)                     
 36CL c  1978St25: thermal neutrons were produced from the Brookhaven High Flux 
 36CL2c  Beam Reactor (HFBR). |g rays were detected with a three-crystal        
 36CL3c  (Ge(Li)-NaI) pair spectrometer. Measured E|g, I|g. Deduced %I|g. Report
 36CL4c  76 |g rays. The authors obtained their reported absolute I|g values by 
 36CL5c  normalizing the sum of 6111|g, 6620|g, 6628|g, 7414|g and 8579|g       
 36CL6c  intensities to that of 1976Sp06. Their values are considered less      
 36CL7c  independent and are not considered for average by the evaluator. An    
 36CL8c  additional 0.2 keV uncertainty is not included in the reported         
 36CL9c  uncertainties as noted in 1978St25 and has been added in quadrature by 
 36CLAc  the evaluator                                                          
 36CL c  1972Lo26: thermal neutrons from the Argonne research reactor CP-5. |g  
 36CL2c  rays were detected with a Ge(Li) detector. Measured E|g, I|g. Report 16
 36CL3c  |g rays (relative and absolute intensities). Absolute %I|g values were 
 36CL4c  obtained by measuring |g rays of {+35}Cl(n,|g) mixed with              
 36CL5c  {+207}Pb(n,|g) and using the ratio of the known cross-sections of two  
 36CL6c  reactions.                                                             
 36CL c  1971Fu06: thermal neutrons were produced from the 1-MW research reactor
 36CL2c  of the Casaccia Centre, Italy. |g rays were detected with a pair       
 36CL3c  spectrometer consising of a Ge(Li) diode and two NaI(Tl) crystals.     
 36CL4c  Deduced levels, J, |p, |g-ray branching ratios. Report 152 |g rays (no 
 36CL5c  uncertainties for I|g)                                                 
 36CL c  1970Ho35: thermal neutrons were from Nuclear Research Institute,       
 36CL2c  Czechoslovakia. |g rays were detected with a Ge(Li) detector. Deduced  
 36CL3c  levels, |g rays branching ratios for |g rays from 1951 and 1959 levels.
 36CL4c  See also 1971Ho30 of the same group for |g(lin pol) measured using a   
 36CL5c  NaI(Tl) Compton polarimeter for 788|g and 1165|g.                      
 36CL c  1969Al11: E|<0.5 keV neutrons were produced at Saclay. |g rays were    
