 36CL c  Target J|p(g.s.)=3/2+                                                  
 36CL c  1988Pi07: E=12.3 MeV deuteron beam was produced from the cyclotron of  
 36CL2c  the Nuclear Physics Institute, Czechoslovakia. Target was 50 |mg/cm{+2}
 36CL3c  natural CdCl{-2} on a carbon backing. Reaction products were momentum  
 36CL4c  analyzed with a multi-angel magnetic spectrograph (resolving power     
 36CL5c  E/|DE|?2000). Measured |s(E{-p},|q). Deduced levels, J, |p, L-transfers
 36CL6c  and spectroscopic factors from DWBA analysis using the DWUCK code.     
 36CL7c  Report 77 levels                                                       
 36CL c  1962Ho04: E=7.5 MeV deuteron beam was produced from the MIT-ONR        
 36CL2c  electro-static generator. Target was carbon tetrachloride gas (75.4% in
 36CL3c  {+35}Cl). Reaction products were momentum-analyzed with a broad-range  
 36CL4c  magnetic spectrograph. Measured |s(E{-p},|q). Deduced levels, J, |p,   
 36CL5c  L-transfers. Report 46 level                                           
 36CL c  1971De21: E=7 MeV deuteron beam was produced from the Utrecht tandem   
 36CL2c  accelerator. Target was natural BaCl{-2} on a carbon foil. Reaction    
 36CL3c  products were momentum analyzed with a split-pole magnetic spectrograph
 36CL4c  (FWHM|?8 keV). Measured |s(E{-p},|q). Deduced levels, J, |p,           
 36CL5c  L-transfers, spectroscopic factors from DWBA analysis. Report 15       
 36CL6c  levels.                                                                
 36CL c  Others:                                                                
 36CL c  1983Fr15: E=12.32 and 12.33 MeV deuteron beams were from Nuclear       
 36CL2c  Physics Institute, Czechoslovakia. Measured proton spectra. Deduced    
 36CL3c  reaction Q-value.                                                      
 36CL c  1973Co25: E=1.8-2.5 MeV deuterons were from the 2.5-MeV electro-static 
 36CL2c  accelerator of the Egyptian AEE. Measured excitation functions. Deduced
 36CL3c  average level width.                                                   
 36CL c  1952Ki33: E=6.9 MeV at H. M. Randall Laboratory of Physics, University 
 36CL2c  of Michigan. Measured |s(|q) for g.s.                                  
 36CL cL $Spectroscopic factor C{+2}S is obtained from DWBA analysis by using   
 36CL2cL d|s/d|W(exp)=N|*(2J+1)C{+2}S|*d|s/dW(DWBA)                             
 36CL cL E$From 1988Pi07. The uncertainties appear very small for a (d,p)       
 36CL2cL measurement, but the authors state that their energy levels are        
 36CL3cL believed to be reliable within quoted uncertainties, because they used 
 36CL4cL as many as possible independent calibration data (up to 80 calibration 
 36CL5cL points in about 8 MeV energy interval) from the precise (n,|g) data    
 36CL cL L,S$From DWBA analysis of measured |s(|q) (1988Pi07). L-transfers are  
 36CL2cL also available from 1971De21 and 1962Ho04 and are the same as those    
 36CL3cL from 1988Pi07 where available, unless otherwise noted                  
