 36CL  H TYP=FUL$AUT=Jun Chen and Lijie Sun$CIT=ENSDF$CUT=30-Sep-2026$                        
 36CL  H TYP=FUL$AUT=NINEL NICA, JOHN CAMERON AND BALRAJ SINGH$                 
 36CL2 H CIT=NDS 113, 1 (2012)$CUT=31-Dec-2011$                                 
 36CL c  J{+|p}({+37}Cl)=3/2+                                                   
 36CL c  1975Ri01: E=35 MeV proton beam was produced from the MSU sector-focused
 36CL2c  cyclotron. Target was NaCl (>96.5% enriched) ona carbon backing.       
 36CL3c  Reaction products were momentum analyzed with a split-pole magnetic    
 36CL4c  spectrograph (FWHM=10-18). Measured |s(E{-d},|q). Deduced levels, J,   
 36CL5c  |p, L-transfers and spectroscopic factors from DWBA analysis.          
 36CL d  1975Ri01 supersede 1974RiYW, 1974RiZQ                                  
 36CL c  Others: 1973Kr08 (E=19,20 MeV), 1972Vi04 (E=40 MeV)                    
 36CL c  1973Kr08: E=19 and 20 MeV proton beams were from the Chalk River MP    
 36CL2c  tandem accelerator. Target was NaCl (96.5% enriched) on a carbon       
 36CL3c  backing. Reaction products were detected with a counter telescope of 3 
 36CL4c  silicon detectors (FWHM=30 keV). Measured |S(E{-d},|q). Deduced levels,
 36CL5c  J, |p, L-transfers, spectroscopic factors from DWBA analysis.          
 36CL c  1972Vi04: E=40 MeV proton beam was from the Grenoble variable-energy   
 36CL2c  cyclotron. Reaction products were detected with two counter telescopes 
 36CL3c  of surface-barrier |DE and E detectors (FWHM=85 keV). Measured         
 36CL4c  |s(E{-d},|q). Deduced levels, J, |p, L-transfers and spectroscopic     
