 36CL c  1981Bh04: {+37}Cl(d,t) E=23.35 MeV deuteron beam was produced from the 
 36CL2c  Argonne cyclotron. Target was enriched {+37}Cl on a thin carbon        
 36CL3c  backing. Reaction products were detected with a |DE-E counter telescope
 36CL4c  (FWHM|?140 keV). Measured |s(E{-t},|q). Deduced levels, J, |p,         
 36CL5c  L-transfers and spectroscopic factors from DWBA analysis using the     
 36CL6c  DWUCK code.                                                            
 36CL c  1976Be53: {+37}Cl(pol d,t) E=12.0 MeV polarized deuteron beam was      
 36CL2c  produced from the Wisconsin Lamb-shift polarized ion source and an EN  
 36CL3c  tandem accelerator. Target was 350 |mg/cm{+2} NaCl (90.36% enriched) on
 36CL4c  a carbon backing. Reaction products were detected with four solid-state
 36CL5c  counter telescopes (FWHM=60-80 keV). Measured |s(E{-t},|q), vector     
 36CL6c  analyzing power. Deduced levels, J, |p, L-transfers, spectroscopic     
 36CL7c  factors from DWBA analysis using the DWUCK code.                       
