 36CL2c  Target was 180 |mg/cm{+2} CaCl{-2} (96% enriched) ona carbon backing.  
 36CL3c  Reaction products were momentum-analyzed with a triplet of magnetic    
 36CL4c  lenses. Measured |s(E{-|a}). Deduced levels. |g rays were also detected
 36CL5c  in this measurement. See details in ({+3}He,|a|g) dataset.             
 36CL c  1972Ro10: E=11 MeV {+3}He beam was produced from the 5.5-MV Van de     
 36CL2c  Graaff accelerator at Strasbourg. Target was a self-supporting foil of 
 36CL3c  Cl{-2}Ca (96% enriched {+37}Cl). Reaction products were momentum       
 36CL4c  analyzed with a magnetic spectrograph. Measured |s(E{-|a},|q). Deduced 
 36CL5c  levels, J, |p, spectroscopic factors from DWBA analysis using the DWUCK
 36CL6c  code.                                                                  
 36CL c  1968Br10: E=15 MeV {+3}He beam was produced from the University of     
 36CL2c  Pennsylvania Tandem Accelerator. Target was BaCl{-2} (99.3% enriched). 
 36CL3c  Reaction products were detected with four solid-state detectors for    
 36CL4c  |s(|q) and were analyzed with a magnetic spectrograph for |s(E{-|a}).  
 36CL5c  Measured |s(E{-|a},|q). Deduced levels, J, |p, L-transfers,            
