 36AR c  S(p)({+36}Ar)=8506.98 {I4}, S(|a)=6640.921 {I27} (2021Wa16)            
 36AR c  1996Il02: {+36}K source was produced by the spallation reaction Ca(p,X)
 36AR2c  with a 500 MeV proton beam from the TRIUMF cyclotron on a target of CaO
 36AR3c  power, selectively ionized, and implanted into a self-supporting carbon
 36AR4c  foil. Delayed particles were detected with a silicon surface-barrier   
 36AR5c  detector (FWHM=23 keV) and heavy recoils were detected with a          
 36AR6c  micro-channel plate detector in a back-to-back geometry around the     
 36AR7c  carbon foil. Measured E{-p}, I{-p}, E{-|a}, I{-|a}. Deduced levels,    
 36AR8c  particle branching ratios, log {Ift} values. Comparisons with available
 36AR9c  data.                                                                  
 36AR d  1996Il02 supersede 1997Il03, 1996IlZZ                                  
 36AR c  1976Fr03: {+36}K source was produced by {+36}Ar(p,n) reaction with a 18
 36AR2c  MeV proton beam from the University of Colorado Nuclear Physics        
 36AR3c  Laboratory cyclotron on a {+36}Ar gas target, and transported to a     
 36AR4c  counting system. |g rays were detected with a Ge(Li) detector. Measured
 36AR5c  E|g, I|g, |g(t). Deduced levels, J, |p, parent T{-1/2}, decay branching
 36AR6c  ratios, log {Ift} values. Comparisons with available data.             
 36AR d  1976Fr03 supersede 1974FrZE, 1973FrZO                                  
 36AR c  1980Es01: {+36}K source was produced via {+36}Ar(p,n) with a 20 MeV    
 36AR2c  proton beam from the University of Jyvaskyla MC-20 cyclotron on an     
 36AR3c  implanted {+36}Ar target. Thermalized {+36}K ions were transported to a
 36AR4c  measurement chamber and deposited onto a aluminum-coated mylar tape.   
 36AR5c  Delayed charged particles were detected with Si(Au) surface-barrier    
 36AR6c  detectors (FWHM|?40 keV). Measured delayed E{-p}, I(p), E{-|a}, I{-|a}.
 36AR7c  Deduced levels, particle branching ratios, log {Ift} values. All the   
 36AR8c  observed delayed proton and |a-particle groups have been assigned to   
 36AR9c  transitions leading to the ground states in the respective daughter    
 36ARAc  nuclei.                                                                
 36AR d  1980Es01 supersede 1981HoZO                                            
 36AR c  1972Mi13: {+36}K source was produced by {+36}Ar(p,n) with 15-30 MeV    
 36AR2c  proton beams from the Triangle Universities Nuclear Laboratory         
 36AR3c  Cyclo-Graaff accelerator on a {+36}Ar gas target. |g rays were detected
 36AR4c  with a Ge(Li) detector and positrons were detected with a NE201 plastic
 36AR5c  scintillator. Measured E|g, I|g, excitation function curve of          
 36AR6c  positrons, |b(t), |g(t). Deduced levels, J, |p, parent t{-1/2}, decay  
 36AR7c  branching ratios, log {Ift} values. See also 1971Ja09 of the same group
 36AR8c  for a measurement of parent T{-1/2}                                    
 36AR d  1972Mi13 supersede 1972JaYZ, 1971MiZZ, 1970JaZQ                        
 36AR c  1980Ew01: {+36}K source was produced by the spallation reaction Sc(p,X)
 36AR2c  with a 600 MeV proton beam from the CERN synchro-cyclotron on a ScC{-2}
 36AR3c  target, selectively ionized, separated by the ISOLDE separator, and    
 36AR4c  transported to carbon foil in a counting chamber. Delayed charge       
 36AR5c  particles were detected with silicon surface-barrier detectors.        
 36AR6c  Measured E{-p}, I{-p}, E{-|a}, I{-|a}. Deduced levels, J, |p.          
 36AR d  1980Ew01 supsersede 1978HaYH                                           
 36AR c  1995Yo04: oriented {+36}K produced by optical pumping of {+36}K in     
 36AR2c  {+36}Ar target during 22 MeV p bombardment. Measured |g(|q) anisotropy.
 36AR3c  Deduced nuclear alignment                                              
 36AR c  1967Be11: {+36}K source was produced by {+36}Ar(p,n) with a 23 MeV     
 36AR2c  proton beam from the Michigan State University cyclotron. |g rays were 
 36AR3c  detected with a Ge(Li) detector. Measured E|g, I|g, |g(t). Deduced     
 36AR4c  levels, J, |p, parent T{-1/2}, decay branching ratios, log {Ift}       
 36AR5c  values.                                                                
 36AR c  1972Mo08: {+36}K source was produced by {+36}K(p,n) with a 27 MeV      
 36AR2c  proton from the University of Colorado cyclotron. Measured |g(t).      
 36AR3c  Deduced parent T{-1/2}                                                 
 36AR c  1971Go18: {+36}K source was produced by {+36}K(p,n) at BNL. Measured   
 36AR2c  |b(t). Deduced parent T{-1/2}                                          
 36AR c  The decay scheme is considered fairly complete by the evaluator, except
 36AR2c  for possible unobserved |g transitions from particle-unbound levels    
 36AR3c  which are seen in (p,|g) E=res.                                        
 36AR cE $%I{-p} and %I{-|a} values quoted from 1996Il02 are determined by the  
 36AR2cE authors relative to %I{-p}=330|*10{+-4} {I90} for E{-p}=970 keV measred
 36AR3cE by 1980Es01                                                            
 36AR cE TI,LOGFT$For bound levels up to 8134, each value of the total feeding  
 36AR2cE is from |g-ray intensity balance at each excited level and for unbound 
 36AR3cE levels, each value is the sum of the intensities of all observed decay 
 36AR4cE modes as given under comments but should be considered lower limit due 
 36AR5cE to unobserved intensities of other possible decay modes, like|g decays 
 36AR6cE of resonances observed in (p,|g) E=res. The associated log {Ift} values
 36AR7cE should be considered upper limits.                                     
 36AR cG E,RI$From 1976Fr03, unless otherwise noted. Note that original E|g     
 36AR2cG values reported in 1976Fr03 are already recoil-energy corrected from   
 36AR3cG measured E|g values and the quoted values here are after               
 36AR4cG recoil-decorrection by the evaluator. Quoted intensities are relative  
 36AR5cG to I|g(1970|g)=100. Note that 1972Mi13 and 1967Be11 report %I|g values 
 36AR6cG which were obtained by the authors by normalizing all relative feedings
 36AR7cG (from I|g intensity balnance) to 4178, 4440 and 6612 levels to 100. The
 36AR8cG evaluator has renormalized them to I|g(1970)=100, as quoted under      
 36AR9cG comments.                                                              
 36AR cG M,MR$From Adopted Gammas                                               
 36AR cG E(X),RI(X)$These transitions are not seen in the decay measurement, but
 36AR2cG have been seen as strong branches in other studies. They are included  
 36AR3cG by the evaluator to obtain more accurate decay feedings from |g-ray    
 36AR4cG intensity balance. The quoted energy values are rounded values from    
 36AR5cG Adopted Gammas and intensity values are deduced by the evaluator using 
 36AR6cG the branching ratios in Adopted Gammas and the I|g value of the        
 36AR7cG strongest transition seen in this dataset from each level. A 20%       
 36AR8cG uncertainty is assumed for the branching ratios to used here if an     
 36AR9cG uncertainty is not available.                                          
 36AR cL $E{-p} and E{-|a} values under comments measured in the lab frame are  
 36AR2cL from 1996Il02, unless otherwise noted.                                 
 36AR cL E$Values are from a least-squares fit to |g-ray energies for bound     
 36AR2cL levels up to 8134 and for particle-unbound levels above that, values   
 36AR3cL are from measured E{-p}(lab) and E{-|a}(lab) values under comments,    
 36AR4cL deduced by the evaluator using E(level)=E{-p}(cm)+S(p)({+36}Ar) or     
 36AR5cL E(level)=E{-|a}(cm)+S(|a)({+36}Ar) with S(p)=8506.98 {I4} and          
 36AR6cL S(|a)=6640.921 {I27} (2021Wa16) and assuming all delayed particles go  
 36AR7cL to the ground state of the respective daughter nucleus (1996Il02,      
 36AR8cL 1980Es01). E{-p}(cm) is deduced from                                   
 36AR9cL E{-p}(cm)=E{-p}(lab)|*m({+35}Cl)/[m({+35}Cl)+m(p)], where m({+35}Cl)   
 36ARAcL and m(p) are the atomic masses of {+35}S and proton, respectively, and 
 36ARBcL E{-|a}(cm)=E{-|a}(lab)|*m({+32}S)/[m({+32}S)+m(|a)]                    
