 36AR    37CA ECP DECAY (180.3 MS)     1997KA10,1991GA23,1974SE11ENSDF    202603
 36AR  H TYP=FUL$AUT=Jun Chen and Lijie Sun$CIT=ENSDF$CUT=30-Sep-2026$                        
 36AR  H TYP=ERR$AUT=Balraj Singh$DAT=8-Nov-2013$COM=Fixed NP on N record$      
 36AR  H TYP=FUL$AUT=NINEL NICA, JOHN CAMERON AND BALRAJ SINGH$                 
 36AR2 H CIT=NDS 113, 1 (2012)$CUT=31-Dec-2011$                                 
 36AR c  1997Ka10 (also 1995Ga03,1991Ga23,1990Ga17): note that 1997Ka10 didn't  
 36AR2c  measure {+37}Ca decay but is about {+36}Ar(p,p) measurement. They quote
 36AR3c  a list of unpublished E(level) and B(GT) data from the work by the same
 36AR4c  group, with the same first author as 1995Ga03, and those data are      
 36AR5c  considered to supersede 1995Ga03 and their earlier work, and are quoted
 36AR6c  in this dataset. The following are the details of the decay measurement
 36AR7c  from 1991Ga23. {+37}Ca source was produced from the ISOLDE-3 online    
 36AR8c  isotope separator at CERN. Selected ions were implanted into a gas     
 36AR9c  detector as |DE element followed by a Si E detector of a proton        
 36ARAc  telescope (FWHM=16-keV), surrounded by two NaI detectors. Measured E(p)
 36ARBc  and I(p) of delayed protons from the decay of {+37}K levels, E|g, I|g  
 36ARCc  |b|g-coin, |b|p-coin, |gp-coin. Deduced levels, |G{-|g}/|G{-p} ratios. 
 36ARDc  Comparisons with available data. |gp-coin is used to distinguish       
 36AREc  delayed protons to g.s. and excited dates of {+36}Ar.                  
 36AR c  1974Se11: {+37}Ca source was produced via {+36}Ar({+3}He,X) with E=40  
 36AR2c  MeV {+3}He beam from the Berkeley 88-inch cyclotron on a {+36}Ar gas   
 36AR3c  target. Reaction products were transported through a helium-jet system 
 36AR4c  into a counting chamber. Protons were detected with several |DE-E      
 36AR5c  counter telescopes. Measured E(p), I(p). Deduced levels, |b-delayed    
 36AR6c  proton emission probabilities.                                         
 36AR c  1995Tr03 (also 1997Tr05): {+37}Ca source was produced via              
 36AR2c  {+9}Be({+40}Ca,X) with a 400 MeV/nucleon {+40}Ca beam on a 1 g/cm{+2}  
 36AR3c  {+9}Be target at GSI. Fragments were separated by the projectile       
 36AR4c  fragment separator FRS and implanted into a silicon counter. |g rays   
 36AR5c  were detected with two large-volume Ge detectors. Measured E|g, I|g,   
 36AR6c  E|b, E(p), I(p), |b|g-coin, |bp-coin, |bp(t). Deduced proton resonance 
 36AR7c  levels in {+37}K, |G{-|g}/|G{-p} ratios, decay parent T{-1/2},         
 36AR8c  branching ratios, B(GT) values. Comparisons with available data. Found 
 36AR9c  high |G{-|g}/|G{-p} values and corrected for B(GT) values of p-unbound 
 36ARAc  low-lying levels in {+37}K                                             
 36AR c  2015Su01: {+37}Ca beams were produced via the projectile fragmentation 
 36AR2c  reaction of {+9}Be({+40}Ca,X) with E=69.42 MeV/nucleon {+40}Ca primary 
 36AR3c  beam from the Heavy Ion Research Facility in Lanzhou (HIRFL-RIBLL).    
 36AR4c  Measured Ep, Ip, |b-delayed p|g-coin, decay-time spectra. Deduced      
 36AR5c  parent T{-1/2}, |b-delayed proton decay energies and decay branching   
 36AR6c  ratios.                                                                
