 36AR c  1997Sc14, 2009Sc20: ({+12}C,{+12}C) E{-cm}=10.67-16 MeV {+12}C beams   
 36AR2c  were produced at the Pelletron Laboratory of the University of Sao     
 36AR3c  Paulo. Target was 20 |mg/cm{+2} isotropically enriched {+24}Mg on a    
 36AR4c  thin carbon backing. Charged particles were detected with three        
 36AR5c  telescopes consisting of proportional gas counters followed by Si      
 36AR6c  surface-barrier detectors. Measured |s(E{-cm},|q). Deduced             
 36AR7c  hyperdeformed resonance, resonance parameters, elongated shape isomers,
 36AR8c  cluster configurations from S-matrix analysis. Measurement details are 
 36AR9c  in 1997Sc14 and 2009Sc20 report the results from the analysis of data  
 36ARAc  in 1997Sc14. See also 2009Cs02 about theory of elongated shape isomers 
