 36AR c  1972Ho40 and 1973Ho33: E=0.8-2.3 MeV (1972Ho40) and E=0.8-2.6 MeV      
 36AR2c  (1973Ho33) proton beams were produced from the Utrecht 3 MV Van de     
 36AR3c  Graaff accelerator. Targets were BaCl{-2} (99.3% in {+35}Cl) on        
 36AR4c  tantalum backings. |g rays were detected with a Ge(Li) detectors.      
 36AR5c  Measured E|g, I|g, Doppler-shift attenuations (1972Ho40), and |g(|q)   
 36AR6c  (1973Ho33). Deduced levels, J, |p, lifetimes, |g-ray branchings,       
 36AR7c  multipolarties, mixing ratios. 1972Ho40 report all resonances,         
 36AR8c  E(level), |g branching ratios, and lifetimes, and 1973Ho33 mainly      
 36AR9c  report J|p assignments from |g(|q) data. A 20% systeamtic uncertainty  
 36ARAc  from the stopping power theory has been included in lifetime results.  
 36ARBc  See also 1972Ho26 for data at E(p)=2231 and 2136 (superseded by        
 36ARCc  1972Ho40)                                                              
 36AR d  1972Ho40 supersede 1972HoYI, 1972Ho26                                  
 36AR c  1974Jo02: E=0.4-3.0 MeV protons were produced from the 1.1-MV          
 36AR2c  Cockcroft-Walton accelerator, (E{-p} up to 1.1 MeV) and from the 3-MV  
 36AR3c  Van de Graaff accelerator (E{-p}=1-3 MeV) at the South African Atomic  
 36AR4c  Energy Board. Targets were 94% enriched BaCl{-2} on copper backings. |g
 36AR5c  rays were detected with Ge(Li) detectors. Measured E|g, I|g, |g(|q),   
 36AR6c  Doppler-shift attenuations. Deduced levels, J, |p, lifetimes, |g ray   
 36AR7c  multipolarties, branching ratios, mixing ratios. A 15% systematic      
 36AR8c  uncertainty is estimated for that of the stopping power theory. Also   
 36AR9c  report (p,|g),(p,p):resonances for all resonance data reported in      
 36ARAc  1974Jo02                                                               
 36AR c  1966Er06: E=0.733-2.595 MeV proton beams were produced from the Utrecht
 36AR2c  3 MV Van de Graaff accelerator. Target was BaCl{-2} (99.5% in {+35}Cl).
 36AR3c  |g rays were detected with cylindrical NaI scintillation assemblies.   
 36AR4c  Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g(|q), |g(lin pol). Deduced levels, J, |p, |g-ray
 36AR5c  multipolarties, mixing ratios.                                         
 36AR c  1965Er06: E=0.4-3.1 MeV protons were produced from the Utrecht 850 kV  
 36AR2c  Cockcroft-Walton accelerator. Target was BaCl{-2} (99.5% enriched). |g 
 36AR3c  rays were detected with two cylindrical NaI(Tl) crystals. Measured E|g,
 36AR4c  I|g, |g|g-coin. Deduced levels, |g-ray branching ratios. See           
 36AR5c  also 1965Er07                                                          
 36AR c  2002Ro24: E=1.209 and 1.462 MeV protons were produced from the 7-MV Van
 36AR2c  de Graaff accelerator of the University of Freiburg, Germany. Target   
 36AR3c  was 30 |mg/cm{+2} BaCl{-2} (80% enriched). |g rays were detected with  
 36AR4c  two HPGe detectors. Measured E|g, I|g, |g(|q). Deduced levels, J, |p,  
 36AR5c  |g-ray branching ratios, multipolarities, mixing ratios. Comparisons   
 36AR6c  with shell-model calculations.                                         
 36AR c  1994Il01: E=0.15-0.40 MeV and E=0.30-0.86 MeV protons were produced    
 36AR2c  from the SAMES accelerator at Bochum and from the 1-MV JN Van de Graaff
 36AR3c  accelerator at Toronto, respectively. Targets were {+35}Cl implanted on
 36AR4c  tantalum backings. |g rays were detected with a Ge detector. Measured  
 36AR5c  E|g, I|g. Deduced |g-ray branching ratios.                             
 36AR c  1976Ma40 (also 1976MaZK): E|?2.41 MeV proton beam was produced from the
 36AR2c  Queen's University 4 MV Van de Graaff accelerator. Target was 46       
 36AR3c  |mg/cm{+2} BaCl{-2} (99.4% enriched). |g rays were detected with Ge(Li)
 36AR4c  detectors. Measured E|g, |g(|q), |g|g-coin, Doppler-shift attenuations.
 36AR5c  Deduced resonance levels, J, |p, |g-ray branching ratios. DSAM was     
 36AR6c  measured but was not used in 1976Ma40 to extract the lifetime.         
 36AR c  1976Hu01: E=2.36-2.42 MeV protons were produced from the 3 MV Van de   
 36AR2c  Graaff of Strasbourg-Cronenbourg. Targets were BaCl{-2} (99.3%         
 36AR3c  enriched) on gold backings. |g rays were detected with a Ge(Li)        
 36AR4c  detector. Measured E|g, I|g, |g(|q). Deduced levels, J, |p, |g-ray     
 36AR5c  branching ratios                                                       
 36AR c  1976Gr05: E=0.533 MeV proton was produced from a 800 kV Cockroft-Walton
 36AR2c  accelerator. |g rays were detected with NaI(Tl) detectors. Measured    
 36AR3c  E|g, |g|g|g(|q). Deduced spin for E(p)=533 resonance.                  
 36AR c  1975Sa03: E=1.519 and 2.596 MeV protons were produced from the 4 MV Van
 36AR2c  de Graaff accelerator of Queen's University, Canada. Target was        
 36AR3c  BaCl{-2} (99.32% enriched). |g rays were detected with a Ge(Li)        
 36AR4c  detector. Measured E|g, I|g, Doppler-shift attenuations. Deduced       
 36AR5c  levels, lifetimes. A 20% systematic uncertainty is assumed from the    
 36AR6c  stopping power but is not included in the reported lifetimes by the    
 36AR7c  authors. It has been added in quadrature by the evaluator.             
 36AR d  1975Sa03 supersede 1974SaZQ                                            
 36AR c  1974AlYD: E=2.3-2.5 MeV from the 4 MV Van de Graaff accelerator at the 
 36AR2c  Bordeaux-Gradignan Nuclear Research Centre. Measured E|g. Deduced      
 36AR3c  E(p)=2410 resonance                                                    
 36AR c  1970Ca34: E=2.168 and 2.231 MeV protons at Queen's University. |g rays 
 36AR2c  were detected with a Ge(Li) detector. Measured E|g, Doppler-shift      
 36AR3c  attenuations. Deduced T{-1/2}                                          
 36AR c  1970Th03, 1970Th04: E=0.859, 1.097, 1.129 MeV (1970Th03) and E=1.7-2.6 
 36AR2c  MeV (1970Th04) protons were produced from the 4 MV Van de Graaff       
 36AR3c  accelerator at the Bordeaux-Gradignan Nuclear Research Centre. Target  
 36AR4c  was 95% enriched BaCl{-2}. |g rays were detected with a Ge(Li)         
 36AR5c  detector. Measured E|g, I|g, Doppler-shift attenuations. Deduced       
 36AR6c  levels, lifetimes. 1970Th04 report data for levels up to 4440 level and
 36AR7c  1970Th03 report data for levels above 4440 level.                      
 36AR c  1970Th04 supersede 1970ThZX                                            
 36AR c  1961Ku01: E=0.3-0.9 MeV from the 900 kV Utrecht cascade generator.     
 36AR2c  Measured E|g, I|g. Deduced levels. Report 12 primary transitions to    
 36AR3c  g.s. and 1970 level.                                                   
 36AR c  1960Li15: E=0.5-1.0 MeV from a 1.2-MV Cockcroft-Walton generator.      
 36AR2c  Measured E|g, I|g, |g(|q). Deduced levels, J, |p, |g-ray branching     
 36AR3c  ratios from 736, 819, 861, and 896 keV resonances.                     
 36AR c  1957To32: E=0.8-1.8 MeV. Measured E|g, I|g. Deduced levels, |g-ray     
 36AR2c  branching ratios. Report |g rays from 855, 1483, 1510, and 1580        
 36AR3c  resonances.                                                            
