 36AR    35CL(P,G),(P,P'G),(P,A):RES   1974JO02,1968BO06,1965ER06ENSDF    202609
 36AR  H TYP=FUL$AUT=Jun Chen and Lijie Sun$CIT=ENSDF$CUT=30-Sep-2026$                        
 36AR  H TYP=ERR$AUT=NINEL NICA, JOHN CAMERON AND BALRAJ SINGH$                 
 36AR2 H CIT=NDS 113, 1 (2012)$CUT=31-Dec-2011$                                 
 36AR c  {+35}Cl target J|p(g.s.)=3/2+                                          
 36AR c  S(p)=8506.98 {I4} (2021Wa16)                                           
 36AR c                                                                         
 36AR c  {U(p,|g) resonances:}                                                  
 36AR c  1974Jo02: E=0.4-3.0 MeV protons were produced from the 1.1-MV          
 36AR2c  Cockcroft-Walton accelerator (E{-p} up to 1.1 MeV) and from the 3-MV   
 36AR3c  Van de Graaff accelerator (E{-p}=1-3 MeV) at the South African Atomic  
 36AR4c  Energy Board. Targets were 94% enriched BaCl{-2} on copper backings. |g
 36AR5c  rays were detected with Ge(Li) detectors. Measured |g-ray yields.      
 36AR6c  Deduced resonance levels, strengths. Report 84 resonances.             
 36AR c  1965Er06: E=0.4-3.1 MeV protons were produced from the Utrecht 850 kV  
 36AR2c  Cockcroft-Walton accelerator. Target was BaCl{-2} (99.5% enriched). |g 
 36AR3c  rays were detected with two cylindrical NaI(Tl) crystals. Measured     
 36AR4c  |g-ray yields. Deduced resonance levels, strengths, widths. Report 65  
 36AR5c  resonances. See also 1964Er04                                          
 36AR c  1972Ho40: E=0.8-2.3 MeV proton beams were produced from the Utrecht 3  
 36AR2c  MV Van de Graaff accelerator. Targets were BaCl{-2} (99.3% in {+35}Cl) 
 36AR3c  on tantalum backings. |g rays were detected with a Ge(Li) detectors.   
 36AR4c  Measured |g-ray yields. Deduced resonance levels. Report 20 resonances 
 36AR c  1994Il01: E=0.15-0.40 MeV and E=0.30-0.86 MeV protons were produced    
 36AR2c  from the SAMES accelerator at Bochum and from the 1-MV JN Van de Graaff
 36AR3c  accelerator at Toronto, respectively. Targets were {+35}Cl implanted on
 36AR4c  tantalum backings. |g rays were detected with a Ge detector. Measured  
 36AR5c  |g-ray yields. Deduced resonance levels, strengths (normalized to      
 36AR6c  S{-p|g}=5.6 eV {I8} for E(p)=860 resonance in 1979Pa16)                
 36AR c  1979Pa16 (also 1978Pa03): E=0.5-2.0 MeV protons were produced from the 
 36AR2c  University of Melbourne 5 MV Pelletron accelerator. |g rays were       
 36AR3c  detected with a Ge(Li) detector. Measured |g-ray yields. Deduced       
 36AR4c  resonance strength for E(p)=860 keV resonance. 1978Pa03 normalized     
 36AR5c  resonance strengths to S{-p|g}=3.26 eV {I40} (average of values in     
 36AR6c  1975Sw01, 1974Al04, and 1969Ly04) for E(p)=633-keV resonance in        
 36AR7c  {+27}Al(p,|g){+28}Si; 1979Pa16 used 3.21 eV {I22} and S{-p|g}=3.88 eV  
 36AR8c  {I27} for E(p)=620-keV resonance in {+30}Si(p,|g){+31}P, both from     
 36AR9c  their own measurements, for normalization.                             
 36AR c  1976Ma40 (also 1976MaZK): E|?2.41 MeV proton beam was produced from the
 36AR2c  Queen's University 4 MV Van de Graaff accelerator. Target was 46       
 36AR3c  |mg/cm{+2} baCl{-2} (99.4% enriched). |g rays were detected with NaI   
 36AR4c  crystals. Measured |g-ray yields. Deduced resonance strength, width for
 36AR5c  E(p)=2410 resonance                                                    
 36AR c  1976Hu01: E=2.36-2.42 MeV protons were produced from the 3 MV Van de   
 36AR2c  Graaff of Strasbourg-Cronenbourg. Targets were BaCl{-2} (99.3%         
 36AR3c  enriched) on gold backings. |g rays were detected with a Ge(Li) and two
 36AR4c  NaI(Tl) detectors. Measured |g-ray yields. Deduced resonance levels,   
 36AR5c  strengths.                                                             
 36AR c  1970Ke10: E=4.0-12.5 MeV protons the Erlangen Van de Graaff tandem     
 36AR2c  accelerator. Measured |s(E|g). Deduced resonance levels, widths. No    
 36AR3c  numerical data are reported.                                           
 36AR c  1966En04: E=0.3-2.1 MeV protons from the Utrecht 850 keV               
 36AR2c  Cockcroft-Walton generator and the 3 MeV Van de Graaff generator.      
 36AR3c  Measured |g-ray yields. Deduced strength for E(p)=860-keV resonance.   
 36AR4c  S{-p|g}=3.10 eV {I26} from 1958Sm96 for E(p)=621-keV resonance in      
 36AR5c  {+30}Si(p,|g){+31}P is used for normalization.                         
 36AR c  1961He19: E|?0.2-0.7 MeV at Physikalisch-Technische Bundesanstalt      
 36AR2c  (PTB), Berlin. Measured |g-ray yields. Deduced resonance levels.       
 36AR c  1961Ku01: E=0.3-0.9 MeV from the 900 kV Utrecht cascade generator.     
 36AR2c  Measured |g-ray yields. Deduced resonance levels, strengths.           
 36AR c  1960Li15: E=0.5-1.0 MeV from a 1.2-MV Cockcroft-Walton generator.      
 36AR2c  Measured |g-ray yields. Deduced 4 resonance levels.                    
 36AR c  1957To32: E=0.8-1.8 MeV. Measured |g-ray yields. Deduced 3 resonances  
 36AR d  1976CoYS: E|?2.4 MeV. Measured |g-ray yield. Inaccessible              
 36AR d  1978Va23: compilation of (p,|g):resonances                             
 36AR c                                                                         
 36AR c  {U(p,p'|g) resonances:}                                                
 36AR c  1974Jo02: (p,p'|g) E=0.4-3.0 MeV at the South African Atomic Energy    
 36AR2c  Board. Measured |g-ray yields of 1220|g from the first excited state at
 36AR3c  E=1220 and 1762|g from the second excited state at E=1762 in {+35}Cl.  
 36AR4c  Deduced resonance levels, strengths. Report 53 resonances.             
 36AR c                                                                         
 36AR c  {U(p,p) resonances:}                                                   
 36AR c  1988BrZO (also 1986BrZR,1987BrZT,1989BrZN): (p,p) E=0.6-4.0 MeV at     
 36AR2c  TUNL. Measured proton yields. Deduced resonance levels. The author     
 36AR3c  state about 200 resonances are observed, but no data are reported.     
 36AR c  1971BrXT: (p,p) E=0.6-3.1 MeV. Measured proton yields. Deduced         
 36AR2c  resonance levels, J, |p                                                
 36AR c  1971GuZW (also 1970GuZT): (p,p) E=2.38-2.62 MeV. Measured proton       
 36AR2c  yields. Deduced resonance level, width.                                
 36AR c                                                                         
 36AR c  {U(p,|a) resonances:}                                                  
 36AR c  Also includes {+1}H({+35}Cl,|a) from 2011Mo12                          
 36AR c  1968Bo06: E=0.83-2.93 MeV proton beams were produced from the Utrecht  
 36AR2c  Van de Graaff generator. Targets were 5-50 |mg/cm{+2} BaCl{-2} (99.5%  
 36AR3c  enriched in {+35}Cl) on carbon backings. Charged partiles were detected
 36AR4c  with semi-conductor detectors. Measured |s(|E{-p},|q). Deduced         
 36AR5c  resonance levels, J, |p, strengths. Report 58 resonances.              
 36AR c  1994Il01: E=0.177 and 0.311 MeV protons. Measured |s(E|a). Deduced     
 36AR2c  limits of resonance strengths for E(p)=177- and 311-keV resonances. See
 36AR3c  also 1995Ro22, where |G{-|g}/|G ratios for some resonances populated by
 36AR4c  {+35}Cl({+3}He,d) are determined by measuring deuteron-gated proton and
 36AR5c  |g decay from those resonances with known |g-ray branchings.           
 36AR c  1966Ka18,1967Ka25: E=1.3-3.0 MeV, USSR. Measured |a yields, |s(|q).    
 36AR2c  Deduced resonance levels, J, |p, widths for 25 resonances.             
 36AR c  1960Cl02: E|?1.0-3.1 MeV at Chalk River. Measured |a yields. Deduced   
 36AR2c  resonance at 10.7 MeV, Q-value                                         
 36AR c  2011Mo12: {+1}H({+35}Cl,|a) E=21.70-21.90 MeV {+35}Cl beams were       
 36AR2c  produced by the Holifield Radioactive Ion Beam Facility (HRIBF) at     
 36AR3c  ORNL. |a particles were detected by the SIDAR silicon detector array,  
 36AR4c  in coincidence with heavy recoils detected by a Micron Type S1         
 36AR5c  detector. Measured E|a, yield, |a(|q), particle-|a coincidence. Deduced
 36AR6c  resonance strength for 9117 resonance                                  
 36AR dL $Most of the |G values were rejected by the Recommended Upper Limits   
 36AR2dL for |g-ray Strengths (RUL) reason for which they were not adopted here 
 36AR cL $S{-pp1} and S{-pp2} under comments are from 1974Jo02; S{-p|a0} and    
 36AR2cL width |G are from 1968Bo06, unless otherwise noted.                    
 36AR cL $S{-p|g} values are for resonance strength defined as                  
 36AR2cL S{-p|g}=(2J+1)|G{-p}|G{-|g}/|G and are extracted from measured         
 36AR3cL resonance yields. S{-p|a0} is defined as (2J+1)|G{-p}|G{-|a0}/|G.      
 36AR4cL S{-pp1} and S{-pp2} represent the (p,p') strengths for the proton      
 36AR5cL emission to the first and second excited states in {+35}Cl, denoted by 
 36AR6cL (p,p1) and (p,p2) in this dataset, respectively                        
 36AR cL E$Deduced by the evaluator using E(level)=E{-p}(cm)+S(p)({+36}Ar),     
 36AR2cL where E{-p}(cm) is the proton resonance energy in the center-of-mass   
 36AR3cL frame and is deduced from E{-p} (proton beam energy) in the lab frame  
 36AR4cL given under comments and S(p)=8506.98 {I4} for {+36}Ar from 2021Wa16,  
 36AR5cL unless otherwise noted. E{-p}(cm) is deduced from                      
 36AR6cL E{-p}(cm)=E{-p}(lab)|*m({+35}Cl)/[m({+35}Cl)+m(p)], where m({+35}Cl)   
 36AR7cL and m(p) are the atomic masses of {+35}Cl and proton, respectively.    
 36AR cL J$From 1968Bo06, based on the analysis of their measured |s(|q) of |a0 
 36AR2cL from the resonance, unless otherwise noted.                            
 36AR cL T$LABEL=S{-p|g}                                                        
 36AR cL S$LABEL=E{-p}(lab)                                                     
 36AR cL T,S$From (p,|g) measurement in 1974Jo02, unless otherwise noted. Note  
 36AR2cL that the values reported in 1961Ku01 in units of eV is likely relative 
 36AR3cL strengths.                                                             
 36AR cL E(A),S(A)$Resonance not seen in this study, but populated in           
 36AR2cL {+35}Cl({+3}He,d) (1995Ro22) and confirmed by observation of subsequent
 36AR3cL proton decay in coincidence with deuterons. Quoted E{-p} values are    
 36AR4cL deduced from measured E(level) in ({+3}He,d) and S(p)                  
