 36AR c  1970Mo10: E=12 MeV {+3}He beam was produced from the MP Tandem Van de  
 36AR2c  Graaff at the University of Rochester's Nuclear Structure Research     
 36AR3c  Laboratory. Target was about 30 |mg/cm{+2} thick BaCl{-2} (99.3% in    
 36AR4c  {+35}Cl) on a 165 |mg/cm{+2} gold backing. Reaction products were      
 36AR5c  momentum-analyzed with an Enge split-pole mangetic spectrograph        
 36AR6c  (FWHM=15 keV) and detected in emulsions. Measured |s(E{-d},|q) at      
 36AR7c  |q{-cm}|?10|' to 45|'. Deduced levels, J, |p, L-transfers,             
 36AR8c  spectroscopic factors from DWBA analysis using the JULIE code. The     
 36AR9c  uncertainty in absolute cross-section is 20%.                          
 36AR c  1994Il01: E=15 MeV {+3}He beam was produced from 9-MV FN Tandem        
 36AR2c  accelerator at the University of Notre Dame. Targe was {+35}Cl         
 36AR3c  implanted into a carbon foil. Reaction products were momentum-analyzed 
 36AR4c  with a broad-range magnetic spectrograph. Measured |s(E{-d},|q) at     
 36AR5c  |q{-cm}|?5|' to 55|'. Deduced levels, J, |p, L-transfers, spectroscopic
 36AR6c  factors from DWBA analysis using the DWUCK code. The uncertainty in    
 36AR7c  absolute cross sections is estimated to be 30%.                        
 36AR d  1994Il01 supersede 1993IlZZ                                            
 36AR c  1995Ro22: E=25 MeV {+3}He beam was from the Princeton AVF cyclotron.   
 36AR2c  Target was isotropically pure {+35}Cl. Reaction products were          
 36AR3c  momentum-analyzed with the Princeton Q3D mangetic spectrometer         
 36AR4c  (FWHM|?20 keV). Measured |s(E{-d}), dp- and d|g-coin. Deduced proton   
 36AR5c  resonance levels, width ratios. Same group as 1994Il01. See            
 36AR6c  (p,|g):resonances.                                                     
 36AR c  1994Ve04: E=25 MeV {+3}He beam was from the Orsay MP Tandem Van de     
 36AR2c  Graaff accelerator. Target was natural chlorine. Reaction products were
