 36AR c  1994Fo03: E=35-65 MeV electrons were produced from the Darmstadt Linear
 36AR2c  Accelerator (DALINAC). Target was 98.6% enriched {+36}Ar gas. Scattered
 36AR3c  electrons were momentum-analyzed with a mangetic spectrometer. Measured
 36AR4c  |s(E{-e}). Deduced levels, J, |p, transition strenghts.                
 36AR d  1994Fo03 supersede 1991FoZZ, 1987FoZZ, 1986FoZY                        
 36AR c  1972Fa02: E=39 and 56 MeV electrons were produced from the Naval       
 36AR2c  Research Laboratory 60-MeV Linac. Targets were 47.8 and 45.1 mg/cm{+2} 
 36AR3c  {+36}Ar gas, respectively. Scattered electrons were momentum-analyzed  
 36AR4c  with a mangetic spectrometer. Measured |s(E{-e}) at |q=180|'. Deduced  
 36AR5c  levels, J, |p, transition radii, widths from DWBA analysis.            
 36AR d  1972Fa02 supersede 1971FaZX                                            
 36AR c  1977Fi09: E=65-115 MeV electrons were produced from the acceleartor of 
 36AR2c  he National Bureau of Standards (NBS). Target was enriched {+36}Ar gas.
 36AR3c  Scattered electrons were detected. Measured |s(E{-e}). Deduced levels, 
 36AR4c  J, |p, widths. See also 1976Fi12 for a measurement of nuclear charge   
 36AR5c  radius using (e,e) elastic scattering                                  
 36AR d  1976Fi12 supersede 1976FiZW, 1975CrZS, 1975CrZX                        
 36AR cL $Values of B(M1)|^ and B(M2)|^ are from 1994Fo03, in units of          
 36AR2cL |m{+2}{-N}b{+L-1}                                                      
 36AR cL $Values of |G{-0} (width of the g.s. transition) under comments are    
 36AR2cL from 1972Fa02, unless otherwise noted.                                 
 36AR cL E$From 1994Fo03, unless otherwise noted.                               
