 36K  dE EAV,LOGFT$From BetaShape v2.4 (Jun-2024) 2023Mo21.                     
 36K  c  2001Lo11: {+36}Ca beam was produced from fragmentation of {+40}Ca beam 
 36K 2c  at 95 MeV/nucleon by nickel target using LISE3 spectrometer at GANIL   
 36K 3c  and implanted into a silicon detector. Protons were detected with two  
 36K 4c  additional silicon detectors; |g rays were detected with three Ge      
 36K 5c  detectors. Measured E|g, E|b, |b-delayed E(p), I(p), p|g-coin. Deduced 
 36K 6c  levels, decay branching ratios, log {Ift}, B(GT). {+36}K deduced IAS   
 36K 7c  proton decay features. Comparison with shell model predictions.        
 36K  c  1997Tr05 (also 1995Tr02, 1995Ga16): {+36}Ca source was produced via    
 36K 2c  {+9}Be({+40}Ca,X) with a 300 MeV/nucleon {+40}Ca beam on a 1 g/cm{+2}  
 36K 3c  {+9}Be target at GSI. Fragments were separated by the projectile       
 36K 4c  fragment separator FRS and implanted into a silicon counter. |g rays   
 36K 5c  were detected with two large-volume Ge detectors. Measured E|g, I|g,   
 36K 6c  E|b, E(p), I(p), |b|g-coin, |bp-coin, |bp(t). Deduced proton resonance 
 36K 7c  levels, decay parent T{-1/2}, branching ratios, B(GT) values.          
 36K 8c  Comparisons with available data and shell-model calculations.          
 36K  c  2015Su01: measured |b-delayed protons at Lanzhou. Deduced parent       
 36K 2c  T{-1/2}, %(|e+|b{++})                                                  
 36K  c  2007Do17: measured |b-delayed protons at GANIL. Deduced parent T{-1/2} 
 36K  c  1981Ay01: measured |b-delayed protons at LBNL. Deduced mass excess,    
 36K 2c  parent T{-1/2}                                                         
 36K  d  Theoretical calculations: 1990Br26, 1984Mu25                           
 36K  c  {+36}Ca also decays to {+35}Ar by (|e+|b{++})p with a branching of     
 36K 2c  51.2% {I10} (2007Do11). Others: 56.8 {I13} (1997Tr05) and 54.3 {I15}   
 36K 3c  (2001Lo11), both deduced by the evaluator from the sum of all |e+|b{++}
 36K 4c  feedings to proton-unbound states                                      
 36K  c  The decay scheme is considered complete by the evaluator due to a large
 36K 2c  energy gap of between Q-value=10970 {I40} (2021Wa16) and the highest   
 36K 3c  populated level at E(level)=6787                                       
 36K  cE TI$Values from 2001Lo11 and 1997Tr05 are determined from measured I|g  
 36K 2cE values (not explicitly listed) for proton-bound levels and from        
 36K 3cE absolute proton intensities from proton-unbound levels, which are      
 36K 4cE obtained by dividing the corrected number of |g rays or protons by the 
 36K 5cE number of {+36}Ca ions collected in the implantation detector.         
