 36CA c  2022La10 (also 2021La04): E|?50 MeV/nucleon {+37}Ca secondary beam was 
 36CA2c  produced by fragmentation of a 95 MeV/nucleon {+40}Ca primary beam on a
 36CA3c  2mm {+9}Be production target at GANIL. Fragments were separated by the 
 36CA4c  LISE3 spectrometer. The secondary target was the liquid hydrogen target
 36CA5c  CRYPTA. Charged particles were detected with the MUST2 detector array  
 36CA6c  of six telescopes each consisting of a double-sided silicon strip      
 36CA7c  detector (DSSD) backed by sixteen 4cm thick CsI detectors. Measured    
 36CA8c  excitation functions, proton-deuteron angular correlations. Deduced    
 36CA9c  proton resonance levels, J, |p, proton branching ratios, L-transfers   
 36CAAc  and spectroscopic factors from DWBA analysis using the FRESCO code.    
