 36CA c  2024Dr01: E=73 MeV/nucleon {+37}Ca secondary beam was produced at NSCL.
 36CA2c  The secondary target was a 0.5-mm-thick Be. Reaction products were     
 36CA3c  detected with a setup including the CAESAR array, a Si-CsI(Tl) |DE-E   
 36CA4c  Ring Telescope (RT), a Scintillating-Fiber Array (SFA), and the S800   
 36CA5c  spectrograph. Measured total decay-energy spectra of particle decays.  
 36CA6c  Deduced levels, mass excess using Invariant-mass spectroscopy.         
 36CA7c  Comparisons with available data and theoretical calculations.          
 36CA8c  Systematics of neighboring nuclei. See also 2023Dr01 for measurement of
 36CA9c  proton-decay branching ratio of 3029 level                             
 36CA c  2007Do11 (see also 2007DoZV thesis): E=196 MeV/nucleon {+37}Ca         
 36CA2c  secondary beam was produced by fragmentation of 420 MeV/nucleon primary
 36CA3c  {+40}Ca beam from the SIS synchrotonson on a {+9}Be reaction target at 
 36CA4c  GSI. The secondary target was also {+9}Be. Fragments were separated by 
 36CA5c  the FRS separator. Reaction products were selected using the           
 36CA6c  calorimeter telescope array CATE consisting of Si-CsI(Tl) |DE-E        
 36CA7c  telescopes. |g rays were detected with 15 Cluster Ge detectors, 7      
 36CA8c  six-fold segmented MINIBALL triple Ge detectors, and the HECTOR array  
 36CA9c  of eight large-volume BaF{-2} detectors. Measured E|g, particle-|g     
 36CAAc  coin. Deduced levels.                                                  
 36CA c  2012Bu15: E=60 MeV/nucleon {+37}Ca beam was produced by                
 36CA2c  fragmentation of E=95 MeV/nucleon primary {+40}Ca beam on a carbon     
 36CA3c  reaction target at GANIL. Fragments were selected on the basis of      
 36CA4c  energy loss, magnetic rigidity and time-of-flight using ALPHA          
 36CA5c  spectrometer. The secondary target was a {+9}Be foil. Recoils were     
 36CA6c  identified and selected using the SPEG spectrometer and |g rays were   
 36CA7c  detected with an array of 74 BaF{-2} detectors. Measured E|g,          
 36CA8c  recoil-|g-coin. Deduced levels. See also 2007Bu15, 2007Bu36            
